      en: "Gulu is the largest urban center in Northern Uganda and serves as the administrative and commercial capital of the Gulu District. Located in the Acholi sub-region, the city has undergone a remarkable transformation since the end of the long-running conflict with the Lord's Resistance Army in the late 2000s. Historically a center for agriculture and local trade, Gulu is now a burgeoning hub for non-governmental organizations and regional commerce with South Sudan. The city's infrastructure has seen significant upgrades, including the renovation of Gulu Airport and the expansion of the road network connecting it to the capital. Gulu University provides higher education and research opportunities, focusing on the needs of the northern region's post-conflict development. The local culture is rich in Acholi traditions, music, and dance, which are celebrated during community festivals. As a symbol of peace and reconciliation, Gulu represents the resilience and growth of Northern Uganda.",
